answer.worked:
Let $f$ be the number of 5-cent coins and $t$ be the number of 10-cent coins.

$$\begin{align*}
f + t &= 157 &&\text{(1)}\\
0.05f + 0.1t &= 10 &&\text{(2)}
\end{align*}$$

Multiply (2) by 20.

$$\begin{align*}
f + 2t &= 200 &&\text{(3)}
\end{align*}$$

Subtract (1) from (3).

$$\begin{align*}
(f + 2t) - (f + t) &= 200 - 157\\
t &= 43
\end{align*}$$

Jasmine has 43 ten-cent coins.

